## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): This is where all CMS content is assembled and provided to the entire app via React context. Currently it only accepts static defaultContent and memoizes it — there is no mechanism to subscribe to Contentstack live preview events or merge preview updates into the content reactively. Every component reads content through useContent → useContentstackContext → ContentstackProvider, so this is the causal site that must be enhanced to support live preview.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add Contentstack live preview integration to ContentstackProvider: (1) import and call Contentstack's livePreview utility (e.g., Stack.livePreview or @contentstack/live-preview-utils) to subscribe to preview events, (2) add a useState or useReducer for content that merges live preview patches into defaultContent, (3) replace the useMemo that returns static defaultContent with the live-updated state so that when the CMS sends a preview edit, the context value updates and all 236+ useContent consumers re-render with the new data. The Stack instance from src/services/contentstack.ts must also have live_preview config enabled in its initialization.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`ContentstackFactory`): The ContentstackFactory instantiates queries against the Stack SDK object. The Stack initialization (referenced as Stack in this file) must include live_preview configuration (host, enable: true) for the SDK to emit preview events. Without this config at the SDK level, no live preview data will flow regardless of provider changes.
  - **Minimal fix:** Ensure the Stack object (imported at the top of this file) is initialized with live_preview config: { live_preview: { enable: true, host: 'live.contentstack.com' } } (or the appropriate preview host for this environment). This is a config-level change to the Stack initialization that enables the SDK's live preview event emission, which the ContentstackProvider can then subscribe to.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- When a page URL includes the live_preview query parameter in a preview-enabled market (GO, UP, or MX), the rendered page displays the CMS content associated with that preview session rather than failing or showing a blank page.
- When a page URL does not include the live_preview query parameter, the rendered page displays the normal published CMS content for that market, with no preview or draft content visible.
- During an active live preview session, when an editor changes draft content in the CMS, the rendered page updates to display the changed draft content without the tester manually refreshing the browser.
- When a visitor opens a page with the live_preview query parameter in a market where live preview is not configured, the page still renders the published content normally, with no error message, blank screen, or broken layout.
- When live preview is enabled for a market and the page URL includes the live_preview query parameter, the rendered page displays draft or unpublished CMS content that is not visible on the page without the parameter.
- When a visitor opens a page using an invalid or expired live preview link, the rendered page displays the published content or a graceful fallback state, with no error screen, crash, or display of stale draft content.

